+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6023+) **Barbarian city-site randomization is now tunable:** Base AdvCiv/K-Mod used a random Barbarian city-site multiplier (effectively +0..49%), so a city site valued 1000 could spike up to 1490, and thus may beat a better site of e.g. 1100 or 1200 if they did not have such a lucky random variation gain. While this can add variety, it can make clearly stronger nearby sites (e.g., missing a nearby seafood) lose and place Barbarian cities on weaker sites. AdvCiv-SAS fixes this by disabling such randomization, and makes it tunable if needed (so now the value is 0: disabled, 1000 has no chance of beating a 1001 site outside already existing edge cases). See [KI#177](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#177---fixed-multiple-base-advcivk-mod-barbarian-city-placement-issues-could-produce-poor-captured-city-sites).
